1
00:00:03,144 --> 00:00:12,454
Register a new patient — Patients ▸ Electronic Health Records — Create a patient record properly, so scheduling, billing and the portal all work later.

2
00:00:17,739 --> 00:00:23,270
Patients ▸ Electronic Health Records is the register: every patient the practice knows.

3
00:00:23,270 --> 00:00:30,227
Search accepts a name, an MRN, an email or a phone number.

4
00:00:30,227 --> 00:00:40,479
New Patient opens one form. Required fields are marked; the rest can follow later.

5
00:00:40,479 --> 00:00:49,379
Name, date of birth and gender identify the record. The MRN is generated for you.

6
00:00:49,379 --> 00:01:03,808
The email address is what invites this patient to the portal later — worth getting right at the desk.

7
00:01:03,808 --> 00:01:13,366
Insurance is what claims are built from. A record without it will bill as self-pay.

8
00:01:13,366 --> 00:01:20,508
An emergency contact takes ten seconds now and matters on the worst day.

9
00:01:20,508 --> 00:01:27,570
AureonCare confirms before it writes a new record.

10
00:01:27,570 --> 00:01:35,018
Saved. The patient joins the register immediately, with an MRN assigned.

11
00:01:35,018 --> 00:01:38,150
Searching by surname brings the new record straight back.

12
00:01:38,292 --> 00:01:51,572
What you just did

13
00:01:52,157 --> 00:02:01,157
Health | Efficiency | Growth — More in the Getting Started series — the next video is linked on screen.
